From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:54:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] arm64: dts: apple: t602x: Add USB4 and tunneled PCIe in
 7.1 form

Bring the USB4 nodes of asahi-wip-7.2 (CIO reset controllers, ACIO
pins, mailboxes, ACIO, NHI and its DART for the four ports of a die;
Sven Peter, Janne Grunau) and the lab's tunneled PCIe controllers to
the t602x device trees of this tree, and wire them up on the Mac mini
and Mac Studio boards: aliases for m1n1, the Thunderbolt endpoint of
each Type-C connector, the six PCIe controllers of the Mac Studio.

Two things differ from 7.2. This tree's DART driver takes the DMA
window from "apple,dma-range" on the DART and one cell in "iommus", so
the NHI DARTs are written that way. And nothing outside USB4 is
touched: the 7.2 device trees also converted the display DARTs to five
cells, which makes this tree's display driver crash at boot. The board
level parts of t600x-j375.dtsi are added to t602x-j474-j475.dtsi
instead, because the M1 Mac Studio shares that file and gets no USB4
nodes here.

Check: all 110 Apple device trees build; the diff against the stock
tree touches four files and no display or DART-cell line; the j475d
tree has six ACIO, six NHI and six tunneled PCIe nodes.
